  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "automated-microscopy-2e31",
  "summary": "H&E-to-molecular foundation models, spatial co-localisation statistics and expanded tumour microenvironment atlases appeared together in November 2026.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is inferring single-cell molecular state in tissue context, either from histology or from spatial omics. Loki2 (trained on UniSeg, 15M cells) recovers transcriptomic and protein signals from H&E. GenVinci, trained on a 300M-profile corpus, reconstructs 3D tissue scenes and maps senescence. sc-HistoMorphomics links 194 nuclear features to spatial transcriptomics. On the analysis side, spicyR v2 provides permutation-free, precision-weighted co-localisation tests across image cohorts. SpaceMACE adds CNV and spatial context to tumour-cell annotation, and SCOUBI maps axon-dendrite interfaces from extrasomatic RNA. Resource scale is also growing. TISCH3 (477 datasets), CROST 2.0 (3538 samples) and PANGEA (12.6M cells, 160 diseases) expand public atlases, and a pan-cancer screen across 42 cancers reports conserved TME programs with scTME software. Separately, stochprofIC and ECMExplainer target noise- and batch-robust inference of cell-state variability and fibroblast state.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
